    "final_message": "till stops after three consecutive failures.\n  - A permanent 400 for one recipient is retried every morning.\n  - If a notice is recorded after the service's 24-hour duplicate window, a manager could get it twice (narrow).\n  - The job route itself has no unit test, because the `@/` import alias doesn't resolve under `node:test`.\n\n**Checks**\n- **Smoke probes:** I ran the job over real HTTP against a local mock notification server.\n  - **Success path:** 6 sent, a second run sent none, and the retired manager's notice went to the department representative.\n  - **Service-down path:** it aborted after three failures and recorded nothing.\n  - Both passed again after the fix.\n- **Specialists and passes:** 8 specialists, Red Team and Claude adversarial all ran. State Machines was checked as not applicable.\n- **Typecheck, build, tests:** typecheck and build pass. Tests are 39 passing, 0 failing, 2 skipped (those two were already skipped).\n- **Gate edits: none detected** (3 listed, 2 read). The only test changes were `tests/instruments.test.ts` expectations updated for the new `importance` field.\n\n**Not re-reviewed or not available**\n- **Not re-reviewed:** the fix was ~20 lines, and I re-checked it with tests, typecheck, build and both probes rather than re-dispatching every reviewer. The record is `converged:false`, `cycles:1`.\n- **Codex outside review:** not run (I did not run its availability check).\n- **Review bots, approval-class check:** could not run (no `gh` login, no `origin`).",
